   "daf": "17a",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "רָחֵל שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין עֵז כּוּ׳. אֲתָא רַב אוֹשַׁעְיָא מִנְּהַרְדְּעָא, וְאַיְיתִי מַתְנִיתָא בִּידֵיהּ: רָחֵל בַּת עֵז, וְעֵז בַּת רָחֵל — רַבִּי מֵאִיר מְחַיֵּיב, וַחֲכָמִים פּוֹטְרִין.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «A ewe that gave birth to a goat of sorts» and a goat that gave birth to a ewe of sorts are not subject to the obligation of a firstborn. «Rav Oshaya came from Neharde’a and brought a baraita in his hand:» With regard to an animal that has the appearance of «a ewe» and that was «born to a goat, or a goat» that was «born to a ewe, Rabbi Meir deems» it «obligated, and the Rabbis deem» it «exempt.»"
  }
 ],
